  "content": {
    "id": "p41-25j-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "A finite set $X$ with $n$ elements is given. Odin and Thor each choose a random subset of $X$. Find the probability Thor’s subset is contained in Odin’s.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(\\frac34)^n$.\n\nFor each element, three of the four equally likely membership outcomes satisfy containment.",
      "worked": "Choosing a random subset is equivalent to including each element independently with probability $\\frac12$. For each element there are four equally likely outcomes: Thor only, Odin only, both, or neither.\n\nThor’s subset is contained in Odin’s precisely when no element is chosen by Thor only. Thus three of the four outcomes are allowed for each element. Since membership choices for distinct elements are independent,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{Thor’s subset is contained in Odin’s})&=\\underbrace{\\frac34\\times\\cdots\\times\\frac34}_{n\\text{ factors}}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{Thor’s subset is contained in Odin’s})&=\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
